a major victory and one small step which  could see these shop workers  cashing in the supreme court says  lower-paid asda supermarket staff  predominantly women can compare their  line of work  to higher paid warehouse workers who are  mostly men they haven't won the right to  equal pay but this  is the green light to pursuing their  cause a relief  for former employee wendy great  one step but still a few more to go  we're not back in the victorian age  anymore we're in the 21st century  lawyers representing some 44 000 store  workers  say depot workers get between one pound  fifty and three pounds an hour more  they say their case with gender equality  at its heart  isn't about proving the roles are  similar but that the value of them is  the same  we now go on to argue that the roles are  of equal value  and that means that when you look at the  demands of the roles and the skills that  they need  and the training that they need and so  on that they are of equal value  this is one of the biggest equal pay  claims in the uk  private sector it's not just the workers  inside who will be affected this will  have repercussions  across the industry as a society we do  undervalue work that women tend to  dominate in so if you look at something  like the caring profession  which we've seen throughout the past  year has been an extraordinary force in  this country  massively underpaid for what they do and  that happens time and again throughout  so many sectors that  things that are perceived as women's  work is less well-paid  kate worked for the supermarket for  eight years as one of the claimants  she's determined to get compensation  we could be waiting sort of another  another four years you know even longer  possibly nobody nobody really knows and  i think that's  that's down to asda and how they choose  to proceed and but yeah we're prepared  to wait  a spokesperson from asda told us we are  defending these claims  because the pay in our stores and  distribution centres is the same for  colleagues doing the same jobs  regardless of their gender retail and  distribution  are very different sectors with their  own distinct skill sets  and pay rates both sides prepared for  the long fight ahead  in what will be a historic case ashley  harinac sky news
 

